# CakePHP Scheduling

## Documentation First

Prefer Scheduling `docs/index.md`, `Installation.md`, and `API-Reference.md`. There is no Ignis `search-docs` tool.

## Installation

```bash
composer require crustum/cakephp-scheduling
```

Load Scheduling **and** SignalHandler (required):

```php
$this->addPlugin(\Crustum\Scheduling\SchedulingPlugin::class);
$this->addPlugin(\SignalHandler\SignalHandlerPlugin::class);
```

Publish config, migrations, and bootstrap load:

```bash
{{ assist.cakeCommand('manifest install --plugin Crustum/Scheduling') }}
```

That creates `config/scheduling.php` (copy-safe), copies monitoring migrations, and appends `Configure::load('scheduling')` to bootstrap. Then migrate as needed.

## Defining Schedules

@ignissnippet("Register Schedule", "php")
use Cake\Event\EventManager;
use Crustum\Scheduling\Schedule;

EventManager::instance()->on('Application.buildContainer', function ($event): void {
    $schedule = $event->getData('container')->get(Schedule::class);

    $schedule->command('logs archive')->everyHour();
    $schedule->command('reports generate')->dailyAt('02:00');
    $schedule->call(fn () => null)->everyThirtySeconds();
});
@endignissnippet

Also: `$schedule->exec(...)`, invokable objects, `weekly()->mondays()->at(...)`, `withoutOverlapping()`, `onOneServer()`, timezones — see API reference.

## Running

```bash
{{ assist.cakeCommand('schedule list') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('schedule run') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('schedule test') }}
```

Production: one cron entry invoking `schedule run` every minute (adjust for sub-minute tasks per docs). Local continuous runner: `schedule work` when documented. Pause/resume, background tasks, schedule groups, per-task timezones — see docs / API-Reference.

## Monitoring

Manifest publishes monitoring migrations/tables. Sync/prune/list monitoring commands and Rhythm widget — see docs Monitoring. Task output, hooks, and events: `docs/Integration.md`.

## Testing

No `src/TestSuite` assert trait. Use CLI:

- `schedule list` — registered tasks
- `schedule test "…"` — run a single expression/task safely (Integration.md)
- `schedule run` in controlled environments

Prefer Integration.md over inventing fake Schedule APIs in Pest.

## Common Pitfalls

- Skipping `manifest install` — no app `config/scheduling.php` / published migrations.
- Missing SignalHandler — graceful stop broken.
- No cron — schedules never fire.
- Overlapping heavy jobs — use `withoutOverlapping()`.
- Sub-minute schedules with a once-per-minute cron only — follow docs for the right runner cadence.
